+---
+
+Deleting an agent session could get stuck. This makes it always work.
+
+## What blocked deletion before
+- A runner that wouldn't exit within `stop()`'s 1.5s window forced a
+  "Stopping agent session. Delete it again once it exits." retry.
+- Clearing the issue's agent assignment hard-failed deletion for
+  non-hosts ("Only the host can delete...") or on any write error.
+
+## Changes
+- `AgentRunner::abandon()` forcibly forgets a session: kills the process
+  now, drops its signals so a late `finished` can't re-save the row being
+  deleted, cleans up the worktree, and resets to idle so the pooled runner
+  is reusable.
+- `deleteStoredAgentSession()` now stops a running runner and, if it won't
+  exit promptly, abandons it instead of bailing. Clearing the issue event
+  is best-effort: a non-host or a failed write warns but still removes the
+  local session.
+- `removeWorktree()` tolerates an already-removed worktree (e.g. a runner
+  cleaned up its own on stop) so the combined "delete worktree, branch &
+  agent" action still deletes the branch.
+
+## Verify
+- forkmesh-tests and forkmesh-window-tests pass.
+
-- 
